# Default User Roles

Seed on install; see `permissions.mdc` for semantics.

## Shipped Roles

- `super_admin`: platform manage; all active modules (including `accounts`); all-scope reporting.
- `tenant_admin`: tenant manage; all entitled modules (including `accounts`); entitled-scope reporting.
- `facility_admin`: facility manage; facility modules (including `accounts`); facility reporting.
- `integration_admin`: `integrations` and `reports_audit` manage; those modules' reporting.
- `doctor`: Dashboard, Patient Registry, OPD, IPD, ICU, Nursing, Clinical, Theater, Reports, Settings. No top-level Lab / Radiology / Pharmacy / Discharge — order and review those from Clinical (and related care modules).
- `nurse`: nursing, triage, ward care (IPD/ICU as assigned); diagnostics assist; registry; nursing reporting.
- `receptionist`: `patient_registry`, queues/OPD desk; billing view; reception reporting.
- `accountant`: `accounts` (books desk: journals, GL, patient ledgers, chart, period close), `billing`, `claims`; finance reporting. Must include `accounts:read` and `accounts:write` (and `financial:approve` where already granted).
- `pharmacist`: `pharmacy` dispense and stock; billing view; pharmacy reporting; no Patients registry (`/patients`)—patient details only via pharmacy/dashboard embeds.
- `laboratory_technician`: `lab` specimen and workflow; walk-in lab orders (create/reuse Lab encounters; create patients via create-lab-request when entitled); lab reporting.
- `radiographer`: `radiology` scan acquisition; scan-scope reporting.
- `radiologist`: `radiology` interpretation and review; interpretation reporting.
- `physiotherapist`: `physiotherapy` sessions and workflow; physiotherapy reporting.
- `discharge_planner`: `discharge` coordination; discharge reporting.
- `operations_staff`: `operations` tasks; operations reporting.
- `housekeeper`: `housekeeping` tasks and areas; housekeeping reporting.
- `biomedical_engineer`: `biomedical` equipment maintenance; biomedical reporting.
- `mortuary_attendant`: `mortuary` workflow; mortuary reporting.
- `hr_staff`: `hr` administration; HR reporting; Facility Admin users/roles/permissions tabs (full rights). Must **not** receive `accounts:read` / `accounts:write` or the Accounts desk — payroll may later post summary journals into Accounts without opening `/accounts`.
- `patient`: own patient data only; own-data reporting.
- `visitor_guest`: limited visitor info only; allowed-visitor reporting.

## Accounts role matrix

- **Have Accounts rights:** `accountant`, `super_admin` / platform admins, `tenant_admin`, `facility_admin` (via admin access packs).
- **Do not have Accounts rights by default:** `hr_staff` (and HR role packs), billing-only packs, and other non-admin clinical/ops packs unless Access admin assigns `accounts:*` on a custom role.
- Subscription module `facility-accounts` remains a second gate; role keys alone do not open `/accounts` when the module is not entitled.
- See `prompts/02-accounts/02-roles.md`.

## Administration

- Admins may add custom roles with the same vocabulary.
- Reset must restore this matrix atomically; stay auditable.
- Failed changes must roll back completely.
- UI and API must deny unauthorized menus, actions, workflows.

